# Packages the NixOS package repository holds (hps-starter sync nixos).
# One per line: NAME [OUTPUT], or NAME STORE-PATH. NAME is the nixpkgs package
# name without its version; the release's own store-paths list says which store
# path that is (the one whose closure holds the starter's glibc, that is
# x86_64). With no OUTPUT the default output is meant, else the named one. A
# name that the release holds in several versions is refused as ambiguous: it
# is given as a store path instead, which is used as it stands.
# The repository holds each package's whole closure. ZFS is in the stock
# starter and is not listed. Which node gets which package is
# lib/starter/nixos.roles.
libvirt
qemu-host-cpu-only
open-iscsi
mdadm
targetcli-fb
perl
# The ctrl-exec agent needs Perl modules and openssl (plan step 2).
IO-Socket-SSL
Net-SSLeay
# JSON is pure Perl, so its x86_64 copy cannot be told from the other systems'
# by the glibc test; this is the path the stock starter already holds (the
# exact store path in its own closure), so a node installs it from itself.
JSON /nix/store/pra9339n8dyc3dzd7csid66y4byws0ba-perl5.42.3-JSON-4.10
# openssl: the release holds several versions, and the starter's own copy is
# only the library output (no bin/openssl). The agent calls openssl by name for
# pairing, so the bin output of the starter's own version (3.6.5) is named.
openssl /nix/store/fya253x5ky7rhfz6rkgdwjr1fzf7fy71-openssl-3.6.5-bin
